Specifically, the reward generated by user \( u_t \) for arm \( \bm{a}_t^i \) is modeled as:
\begin{equation}
r_t^i | u_t = g_{u_t,t}(\bm{a}_t^i) + \xi_t^i,
\label{eq:reward_function}
\end{equation}
where \( g_{u_t, t} \) is the \emph{true reward} 
of user \( u_t \) at round \( t \), which maps arm \( \bm{a}_t^i \) to a reward, and \( \xi_t^i \) is a noise term with zero mean, i.e., \( \mathbb{E}[\xi_t^i] = 0 \). Additionally, as in existing works~\cite{ban2021local, gentile2014online}, we assume that the reward \( r_t^i \in [0, 1] \).
